From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove@yandex.ru>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:47:54 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 122/297] Meridian: the window on Windows is dragged and
 resized again

Without a title bar the UI page reaches every edge of the window, and over
the page sits the child window Chromium keeps for it on Windows. That child
answered Windows's hit tests with what the window said, "caption" or a
resize edge, and so got the mouse itself: a child window can be neither
dragged nor resized, and nothing happened. It steps aside for those now
(HTTRANSPARENT), as it already did for the maximize button, and Windows
gives the mouse to the window.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../renderer_host/legacy_render_widget_host_win.cc       | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/content/browser/renderer_host/legacy_render_widget_host_win.cc b/content/browser/renderer_host/legacy_render_widget_host_win.cc
index 41962e6003..5005b78387 100644
--- a/content/browser/renderer_host/legacy_render_widget_host_win.cc
+++ b/content/browser/renderer_host/legacy_render_widget_host_win.cc
@@ -729,6 +729,15 @@ LRESULT LegacyRenderWidgetHostHWND::OnNCHitTest(UINT message,
     // highlighting on the maximize/restore buttons with Win11 snap layouts.
     return HTTRANSPARENT;
   }
+  // Meridian: its browser window has no title bar on Windows, and the page
+  // that is its UI reaches every edge under this window. Where the window
+  // itself answers "caption" (the page's drag areas) or a resize edge, step
+  // aside the same way: Windows then gives the mouse to the window, which can
+  // be dragged and resized by it; this child window can't.
+  if (hit_test == HTCAPTION ||
+      (hit_test >= HTLEFT && hit_test <= HTBOTTOMRIGHT)) {
+    return HTTRANSPARENT;
+  }
   return hit_test;
 }
 
